# TRANSITIONS ONLY, from scripts/watch-convergence.sh, over the cycle of 2026-08-11.
# The per-sample logs (three streams, 2 s interval, about 90 minutes) stayed on the
# devbox at /tmp/phase28/; what is evidence is the transitions and the two instants
# this session wrote itself, and those are here verbatim.
#
# READ THE SAMPLING REGIME BEFORE THE NUMBERS. Polling every two seconds keeps a
# fresh copy at the edge at all times with a full TTL ahead of it, so a write can
# never find the edge empty and the delay is uniform in [0, 60]. A visitor who does
# not poll often finds nothing cached and gets the object at once. Both are below.
#
# Columns: mark sighting status age x-cache etag write->edge edge->here window sha
# `::` baseline, `**` transition. The two computed columns are empty here because
# the version that took these readings conditioned them on `Age`, which CloudFront
# omits on a MISS - the response that first carries a new object. That is ADR-0062
# D3; the figures below were reconstructed from head-object afterwards and are
# stated as such.

